0071-4bc9-b0d8-ba30742614f9","position":{"commit_sha":"9399a0456cfb6929e3d24e86a1f8de83a29bf861","position":"1787416376968201001-16ff6a5e-0071-4bc9-b0d8-ba30742614f9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ccf56f95ef48b22264f059d42bf44371f6b05a720fd53d37d08e2bf9cea9192c","event_uuid":"a7f6aab3-b5ba-4341-aa34-0d98ed0b52c2","position":{"commit_sha":"0c19db628fa8d18a9ca686a2dbb8bdb1fb78c5f8","position":"1787417208858184001-a7f6aab3-b5ba-4341-aa34-0d98ed0b52c2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-239_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"e50ec61e-3a77-4eb8-b56b-c1d0f90ff9bc","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"PARKED at operator request. Progress is preserved as a LOCAL COMMIT; nothing is lost, and nothing has been pushed.\n\nSTATE\n- Worktree: /Users/joeoakhart/impl-77e7, branch impl-77e7, working tree CLEAN.\n- Commit 4b9ca707880 'Validate caused_by targets before recording' - 16 files, +454/-76, including the new tests/unit/test_caused_by_link_validation.py. It was uncommitted when the work stopped; I committed it so a stray checkout or worktree cleanup cannot lose it. The commit message states plainly that it is a WIP checkpoint.\n- NOT pushed to Gerrit. There is no change number for this ticket yet.\n- Plan-review attestation: certified.\n- Acceptance criteria: 8, all UNTICKED and NOT yet verified.\n\nWHAT IS VERIFIED\nmake lint, make typecheck (630 files) and the complexity ratchet (new=0 increased=0) all pass. 50 tests green across tests/unit/test_caused_by_link_validation.py, tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_applier_inbound_links.py and tests/interfaces/facades/test_parity.py. That is the extent of it - the gates and those suites, nothing more.\n\nWHAT IS NOT DONE\n- The 8 acceptance criteria are unverified. Do not tick them without running each criterion's own stated command; inventing a paraphrase produced false results twice in this epic.\n- file_impact is NOT reconciled against the actual diff. The close gate refused SIX tickets in this epic for exactly this (1cf6, 7931, a73e, d6e3, 1dd5, 73b8). Run rebar set-file-impact from the real diff AFTER implementation is final, not before.\n- No mutation evidence has been gathered for the new test.\n- The change has never been through code review or CI.\n\nTO RESUME: cd /Users/joeoakhart/impl-77e7, export PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\", amend or extend 4b9ca707880, then follow /Users/joeoakhart/.claude/jobs/e50ec61e/tmp/LEAF_BRIEF.md from its section 4. The ticket stays in_progress because real work exists and is claimed - it is parked, not abandoned.","timestamp":1787417208858184001}],"created_at":1787354787501040001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ae593429-4aae-4e68-a552-d84360f3dddf","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"50e3-6d2a-0e7f-4e92"},{"link_uuid":"790ceac1-240f-4e07-807d-418797594b03","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a4d7-ee6a-99ba-423e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`caused_by` is the store's only machine-readable causation edge and it is not trustworthy:\n`rebar link <bug> <target> caused_by` accepts ANY target, so `rebar metrics`\n(`bug_caused_by_fan_in`) and the epic-close `caused_by` floor reason over edges nobody\nvalidated. The most-linked target today is a misattribution whose \"children\" are unrelated\nCI items.\n\nVerified against `origin/main` first: `rebar link` validates only relation grammar, cycles,\nthe redundant-link guard and the closed-source guard (`graph/_links.py:add_dependency`), and\nhas NO `--force`. The \"does a commit reference this ticket?\" scan exists exactly once,\nprivately, as `_referencing_commits` in `_commands/close_precheck.py`; its `[]` return\nconflates \"scanned, none found\" with \"no git history\".\n\n## Approach\n\n1. Hoist the trailer/subject scan into the existing shared module\n   `_engine_support/commit_impact.py` as `referencing_commits(ids, tracker, repo_root)`\n   returning `list[str] | None`, `None` = \"git history unreadable\" — the same `None`-vs-`[]`\n   distinction `changed_paths` there already uses. `close_precheck._referencing_commits`\n   becomes a thin `... or []` delegate KEEPING ITS NAME (a string monkeypatch target in\n   `tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py`); `_referencing_commit_exists` — re-exported by\n   `transition_close` and asserted directly in `tests/unit/test_transition_close.py` — still\n   delegates to it, so both keep their current contracts.\n2. Add ONE predicate `caused_by_refusal(target_id, relation, tracker, code_root) -> str | None`\n   in `_commands/link_revert.py`. BOTH `link_core` (the write) and `_link_dry_run` (the\n   preview) call it: `_link_dry_run` does not route through `link_core`, so a shared\n   predicate — not a shared code path — is what stops the preview drifting from the refusal.\n3. The rule: for `caused_by`, the RESOLVED TARGET must have >=1 referencing commit — the\n   target ITSELF, not its descendants, because `caused_by` must name the specific change that\n   introduced the defect and crediting an epic through its children is the exact\n   misattribution this story exists to stop. `caused_by` is never hierarchy-promoted, so the\n   resolved target is the requested one.\n4. Command layer, not `add_dependency`: `rebar.graph` is the store layer, runs NO git and\n   takes no `repo_root` (only `tracker_dir`), and `link_core` is its only functional caller.\n   Both callers resolve the CODE root as `config.repo_root(repo_root)` and pass THAT — never\n   the tracker dir, which an absolute `tracker.dir` can relocate — mirroring close_precheck's\n   `code_root`/`tracker` split.\n5. Unverifiable is NOT invalid: `None` from the scan (no code repo / no commits) allows the\n   link. A refusal must mean \"this target has no commit\", never \"this clone has no history\".\n6. Escape hatch `--force[=<reason>]` on the CLI, `force=` on library and MCP, spelled as\n   `claim --force`. Its parser moves to `_cli/_parsers/core/writes.py:extract_force` and\n   `claim._parse_force` delegates, so the CLAIM-STYLE spelling has one implementation shared\n   by claim and link. `transition._extract_force` and `tracker_maintenance` keep theirs:\n   transition's bare `--force` yields `''`, not `'(no reason given)'` — a different contract.\n7. Reconciler: `_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py:337` applies arbitrary\n   inbound relations through `rebar.link` and fails open, so a peer-authored `caused_by` whose\n   commit lives only in another clone would be dropped and recorded as an impossible link.\n   That call passes `force=\"inbound reconcile: peer-authored edge\"`; sync is unchanged.\n8. Oracle: a `\"link\"` branch in `write_parity_contract.execute()` (and `Case.op`), plus `link`\n   on the Adapter protocol and all three adapters changed from `(a, b, relation) -> None` to\n   `(a, b, relation, *, force=None) -> Outcome`. `adapter.link` IS called, at\n   `tests/interfaces/facades/test_parity.py:147` (`test_deps_parity`), which discards the\n   return; that file joins Scope and gains `assert adapter.link(a, b, \"blocks\")`.\n9. `SKILL.md`: the rule governs the `rebar link ... caused_by` form (CLI/library/MCP) ONLY —\n   the close's `--caused-by=<id>` flag writes via `transition_close._apply_caused_by` and is\n   NOT gated. Say that at the early-link instruction (~L598-607) AND at the Omission case\n   (~L633-644), whose scope-of-work story/epic target is commit-less by construction, with\n   the worked example `rebar link <bug> <story> caused_by --force=\"scope-of-work attribution:\n   the story that should have covered this case has no introducing commit\"` plus a note to\n   repeat that reason in the RCA. Unattributable still leaves the link unset.\n\n## Scope\n\n`src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`,\n`src/rebar/_commands/link_revert.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/writes.py`,\n`src/rebar/_cli/help/link.txt`, `src/rebar/_commands/claim.py`,\n`src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py`,\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_caused_by_link_validation.py` (new), `tests/interfaces/adapters.py`,\n`tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_parity.py`,\n`docs/ticket-model.md`, `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md`.\n\n## Explicitly OUT of scope\n\nThe original plan's `introducing_sha` field + `rebar fsck` date check and the \"attach the\n196-row corpus\" criterion are cut and re-filed as a follow-up linked `discovered_from`: no\nsurface writes `introducing_sha` so it would land dead; `fsck` is a STORE-integrity walker\nthat must run where no code repo exists; the corpus is absent from the repo.\n\n## Testing\n\nNew `tests/unit/test_caused_by_link_validation.py`, over a store whose code repo has real\ncommits: happy path (a target carrying a `rebar-ticket:` trailer commit links); refusal (the\nerror names the target and `--force`; `show_ticket(...)[\"deps\"]` unchanged); `force=\"...\"`\nrecords the edge; `relates_to`/`blocks` to the same target unaffected; a commit-less code\nrepo allows the link; `--dry-run` prints \"Would reject\" and writes nothing;\n`close_precheck._referencing_commits` still resolves by name and still returns `[]`.\n\nPinning: `tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py`, `tests/unit/test_transition_close.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_caused_by_dedup_10d0.py`, `tests/unit/test_epic_bug_screen_4b54.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_close_gate_*.py`, `tests/unit/test_claim_*.py`,\n`tests/interfaces/facades/test_parity.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A `caused_by` link to a commit-less target is refused identically on library, CLI and\n      MCP, `force` bypassing it on all three; two new `op=\"link\"` rows make\n      `pytest tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py -q` cover it.\n- [ ] The refusal names the target and the escape hatch, leaves the store unwritten, previews\n      under `--dry-run`, and allows a commit-less code repo; checked by\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_caused_by_link_validation.py -q`.\n- [ ] The scan has ONE implementation:\n      `test $(grep -cE '%H%x1f' src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py) -eq 0`.\n- [ ] The delegate keeps its name:\n      `test $(grep -cE '^def _referencing_commits' src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py) -eq 1`.\n- [ ] The close gate is behaviour-identical:\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py tests/unit/test_transition_close.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py -q`.\n- [ ] Docs state the rule: `grep -q 'referencing commit' docs/ticket-model.md` (absent today).\n- [ ] SKILL.md carries the forced-link example:\n      `test $(grep -c 'scope-of-work attribution' examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md) -eq 1`.\n- [ ] Gates green: `make lint`; `make typecheck`;\n      `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reporting `new=0 increased=0`.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py","reason":"shared referencing-commit scan"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","reason":"delegate to the shared scan"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/link_revert.py","reason":"caused_by refusal predicate + --force"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/writes.py","reason":"--force on build_link + shared extract_force"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/link.txt","reason":"regenerated help text"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/claim.py","reason":"_parse_force delegates to the shared extractor"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py","reason":"link(force=) library param"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"link_tickets(force=) MCP param"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py","reason":"inbound link applies with force"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_caused_by_link_validation.py","reason":"new behavioural tests"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/adapters.py","reason":"link adapter returns an Outcome and takes force"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py","reason":"link parity rows"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_parity.py","reason":"test_deps_parity asserts the new Outcome"},{"path":"docs/ticket-model.md","reason":"document the caused_by rule"},{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md","reason":"Omission-case forced-link example"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","a4d7-ee6a-99ba-423e"],["parent","2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a"],["relates_to","50e3-6d2a-0e7f-4e92"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","parent_status_uuid":"fc0349c5-2a1a-4527-a93a-4812af1563fd","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["gates","fortnight-review"],"ticket_id":"77e7-1eec-7b52-46ed","ticket_type":"story","title":"Refuse a caused_by link whose target has no referencing commit","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["790ceac1-240f-4e07-807d-418797594b03","44d753e5-507d-461b-98a5-ac9126bbda14","f146335b-0d6b-4b91-8016-1d17b030366d","feec4340-1c75-4c35-ad4d-29e3c136ec61","0f74ed91-cd38-4a05-a41c-246d58e1cd56","b03a84bb-856a-4f7f-90aa-1f10c5826c47","bbe5333c-b8fd-4eee-aeca-8024699dabcc","e36f2